supabase/.temp/

# migration working files (2026-08-14)
#
# The blanket rule is for the singapore->frankfurt dump files in the repo root
# — schema.sql, data.sql, data-wrapped.sql, auth-data.sql and the two
# trigger toggles — which are heavy, one-off, and must stay out.
#
# But it is blanket, so it also swallowed supabase/migrations/*.sql, and a
# migration that vanishes into a silent ignore makes no noise anywhere: it runs
# in the database, the ledger records it, and the file simply is not in git.
# Every migration from 0059 on had to be forced in with `git add -f`, and 0066
# was nearly lost that way on 2026-08-30 — a plain `git add` skipped it without
# a word. The exception below removes the need to remember the flag.
#
# (0052, the one migration actually missing, predates this rule by nine days —
# it was pasted by hand and never saved as a file at all. Different cause, and
# not one a .gitignore change could have prevented. See docs/BACKLOG-V1b.md.)
*.sql
!supabase/migrations/*.sql
# ...and the verify queries beside them. Rule 50 sends every migration's
# verification here, and until 2026-09-17 the negation above did not reach the
# folder — so each one was ignored by default and survived only if somebody
# remembered `git add -f`. 0087_verify.sql is tracked; nothing guaranteed the
# next one would be. Same failure mode as the missing 0052, same one-line cure.
!supabase/verify/*.sql
baseline-*.txt
new-rows.txt
seq-*.txt

# local machine markers (git-repo-guard opt-in) — not shared
.claude/
